From 726ae3a688ff6b4dbe855f1412ed448e169e79cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:28:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: HD textures for Sonic Riders and Tournament Edition
 (Mods & expansions)

Mods & expansions gets an HD TEXTURES section, one row per online game (Sonic Riders,
Tournament Edition): "Choose the pack's folder..." installs a texture pack the player has (a
folder of tex1_*.png/.dds, in subfolders) as the file mod srnp_textures_hd_<disc ID> (textures/,
then mod.ini, game=<disc ID>), turned on; its switch is also in the list of mods. The textures are
hard-linked into the user folder's Mods when the pack is on the same drive (no extra space), else
copied there once, so that the runtime's cache (Cache/textures, hard links) and the online game
folder can link them in turn. Tournament Edition can "Use Sonic Riders' pack": its textures are
named after the ones they replace, so it dresses the textures TE shares. A pack folder that holds
the Mods folder is refused. --hd-textures <disc ID> <folder> does the same without the window.
The online game folder hard-links the mods' files when it can (a pack is hundreds of MB), copies
them otherwise.

Measured 2026-11-26 (no game started): Sonic Riders' HD pack (Gigapixel AI + Waifu Caffe), 3197
textures, all hard-linked; the same for TE from Sonic Riders' mod; a folder with no texture and a
folder holding Mods are refused.

